{"name":"China Doll","hex":"#f3e4d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"china doll","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of doll made at least partly out of glazed porcelain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china_doll"}],"entries":[{"title":"China doll","blocks":[{"text":"A china doll is a doll made partially or wholly out of glazed porcelain. The name comes from china being used to refer to the material porcelain. Colloquially the term china doll is sometimes used to refer to any porcelain or bisque doll, but more specifically it describes only glazed dolls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/China_doll_heads%2C_1750-1870_-_Fairbanks_Museum_and_Planetarium_-_DSC04299.JPG/330px-China_doll_heads%2C_1750-1870_-_Fairbanks_Museum_and_Planetarium_-_DSC04299.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_doll"},{"title":"China Doll (play)","blocks":[{"text":"China Doll is a two-act play by David Mamet about political corruption and brutal violence. The play opened on Broadway at the end of 2015 with a short run scheduled to close at the end of January 2016. The two-act play contains only two characters who appear on stage throughout the play, Mickey and Carson."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Doll_(play)"},{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"},{"title":"Doll","blocks":[{"text":"A doll is a model typically of a human or humanoid character, often used as a toy for children. Dolls have also been used in traditional religious rituals throughout the world. Traditional dolls made of materials such as clay and wood are found in the Americas, Asia, Africa and Europe. The earliest documented dolls go back to the ancient civilizations of Egypt, Greece, and Rome. They have been made as crude, rudimentary playthings as well as elaborate art. Modern doll manufacturing has its roots in Germany, from the 15th century. With industrialization and new materials such as porcelain and plastic, dolls were increasingly mass-produced. During the 20th century, dolls became increasingly popular as collectibles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Poup%C3%A9e_c_1870.jpg/330px-Poup%C3%A9e_c_1870.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doll"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Chinadoll.jpg/500px-Chinadoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Chinadoll.jpg/500px-Chinadoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Typical German 1860s flat top hair style china doll","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChinadoll.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d5/KPMdoll.jpg/250px-KPMdoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d5/KPMdoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d5/KPMdoll.jpg/250px-KPMdoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rare c.1840s KPM china doll","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKPMdoll.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/C.2000s_American_ceramic_copy_of_antique_German_china_doll_head.jpg/330px-C.2000s_American_ceramic_copy_of_antique_German_china_doll_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/C.2000s_American_ceramic_copy_of_antique_German_china_doll_head.jpg/330px-C.2000s_American_ceramic_copy_of_antique_German_china_doll_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reproduction china doll head with characteristic poorly painted appearance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AC.2000s_American_ceramic_copy_of_antique_German_china_doll_head.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Japanesereproductions.jpg/500px-Japanesereproductions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Japanesereproductions.jpg/500px-Japanesereproductions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mid-20th century labeled Japanese reproduction doll heads, made in both glazed porcelain and Parian, and in both blonde and black hair.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJapanesereproductions.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219959.jpg/500px-MET_DP219959.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/MET_DP219